eom_point(size = 2.5) +</div><div>   labs(x = &quot;Day of analysis&quot;, y = &quot;pH&quot;, color = &quot;&quot;)</div></div><div><br clear=\"none\"></div></div><div><div><br clear=\"none\"><div>On Thu, Feb 26, 2015 at 8:27 PM, &#39;Shittu, Aminu&#39; via ggplot2 <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\" shape=\"rect\" href data-email-masked>ggp...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br clear=\"none\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div style=\"color:#000;background-color:#fff;font-family:garamond,new york,times,serif;font-size:14px\"><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,&#39;Segoe UI&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Dear ggplotters,</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,&#39;Segoe UI&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><br clear=\"none\"></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,&#39;Segoe UI&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">For a beginner practising multiple line plotting in R, using the below few data. </span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,&#39;Segoe UI&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Included below the data is the desired graph output, created in Microsoft Excel.</span></div><div style=\"font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,&#39;Segoe UI&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" width=\"192\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:144pt\"><colgroup span=\"1\"><col span=\"3\" width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\"></colgroup><tbody style=\"width:192px\"><tr height=\"20\" style=\"min-height:15pt\"><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" height=\"20\" width=\"64\" style=\"min-height:15pt;width:48pt\">Days</td><td colspan=\"1\" rowspan=\"1\" width=\"64\" style=\"width:48pt\">Mussel